Reproduce hangs after abandoned pod launches

Readiness waits can retain a pod's lifecycle lock after the launching
CLI exits. An open event stream without a state greeting, or retries
after the container stops, then block later delete and enter requests
forever.

Use a controlled startup hook to reproduce both states without assuming
what originally stalled the affected pods. A passing release control
checks the fixture, while three regression tests require recovery within
15 seconds and currently fail against the unfixed daemon. Bound and reap
test commands so these failures report the hang instead of hanging the
test runner. No production behavior is changed.

Validation: all four required smoke filters passed via cargo pipeline.
cargo pipeline readiness_wait passed the release control and reproduced
all three hangs on both attempts, with no test runner timeouts.
